 data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">join Machine Engineer Society</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">give suggestions</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">stay up to date</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">make important contacts</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_5_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3126760-recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_5_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>An Overview of The Research on Amber</strong></p><p>Amber: a fossilised tree resin, which may be produced to protect itself against <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and fungi.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Colors</strong></p><ul><li>usual yellow, orange, or brown</li><li>uncommon colors e.g. blue (what causes the blue color in amber is related to the occurrence of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>)</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Formation</strong></p><ul><li>under sustained <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and pressure</li><li>during an <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> stage between resins and amber, copal is produced.</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Places and Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>commonly found on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> e.g. in Russia</li><li>avoid exposure to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, rain, and temperate extremes</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Inclusions</strong></p><ul><li>Dominican amber: 1 inclusion to every 100 pieces</li><li>Baltic amber: 1 inclusion to every <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> pieces</li></ul><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>Uses and Applications</strong></p><ul><li>It can be used to make ornamental objects and jewelry in <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> settings.</li><li>Some people believe that its powder mixed with <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> cures throat, eye and ear diseases.</li><li>It has even been used as a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> material, for instance using it to create Amber Room.</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/recent_actual_test_2_academic_listening_test_5_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q1","part_id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Greenway","correct_answer_variants":["Greenway"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3126681_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q2","part_id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-p1","group_id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"pk2@cat.com","correct_answer_variants":["pk2@cat.com"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3126681_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-practice-source-2-t5-l-q3","part_id":"en-practice-sour